From ba31e70527f861b2811576e37b2010f1c4957e67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:01:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] split EPPKE from MRSNO - DPP SecurityIEs - Airties DPP relay
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Split eppke (802.11bi EPPKE) out of additional_auth into its own flag
so it and MRSNO/RSN Overriding are tracked independently through
agent<->ap_manager IPC, WSC, UCI, and the nl80211 HAL.

Extend DPP onboarding with MRSNO support, mirroring the WSC M2 path:
Controller emits "SecurityIEs" as a root-level sibling of "cred" in
the Configuration Object (cred.akm left empty when used), only to
agents that advertised RSN Overriding in their AP Capability TLV
(agent->rsn_overriding_supported); eppke and SecurityIEs stay mutually
exclusive for now. Agent decodes SecurityIEs back through the existing
UCI/hostapd path. Also fixes a TLVF field-ordering bug where
security_ies must be allocated before enabled_ecp_groups/
security_profiles/rsnxe_capab_mask on cEncryptedSettingsPayload.

Per EasyMesh §17.1.54, the agent now also handles the optional Default
802.1Q Settings TLV and Traffic Separation Policy TLV on the BSS
Configuration Response, ahead of sending the BSS Configuration Result.

Add em_ap_controller_found: propagated from the M2 Supported Service
TLV through ap_manager to sBssInfoConf, so a BSS onboarded by a
non-standard controller (e.g. Airties, which never sets WSC_AUTH_DPP
in its M2 AKM) still gets the local DPP-over-TCP relay config written
into UCI/hostapd.

Signed-off-by: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
